      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think is unnecessary and confusing? \n\nWhen testing a single class, isn\u0027t it standard practice to have one test class covering all the test cases for that class? Similarly, I want to keep all LE scan tests in LeScanningTest class without creating a new test class for each LE scan test case.\n\nTherefore, I am adding Parameterized LE scan tests to LeScanningTest and as a result have to separate the non parameterized and parameterized tests into separate inner classes, due to the nature of Parameterized tests config. Moreover, the non parameterized and parameterized tests share a lot of common logic, so this avoids code duplication.\n\nIf you still feel strongly about it, let me know and I can revert it to create a new class for parameterized test cases instead as I understand that each team may have their own preferences.\n\nWhen you said that the latter CL adds a lot of logic on top of test logic, what are you referring to? That CL is a WIP, so let me know and I can try to address now if something doesn\u0027t look right. Also, how does it matter if it is in this class or in a separate class  if bugs are introduced anyways?",
